1
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:21,000
What went on the screen was nothing compared to what went on behind the scenes.

2
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,000
RKO 281 is a drama, history, tv movie film directed by Benjamin Ross.

3
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:51,000
In 1939, boy-wonder Orson Welles leaves New York, where he has succeeded in radio and theater, and,
hired by RKO Pictures, moves to Hollywood with the purpose of making his first film.

4
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Orson Welles, played by Liev Schreiber.

5
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
William Randolph Hearst, played by James Cromwell.

6
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Marion Davies, played by Melanie Griffith.

7
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Herman Mankiewicz, played by John Malkovich.

8
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Gregg Toland, played by Liam Cunningham.

9
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
Louis B. Mayer, played by David Suchet.

10
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
RKO 281 is a 1999 American historical drama television film directed by Benjamin Ross, written by John Logan, and
starring Liev Schreiber, James Cromwell, Melanie Griffith, John Malkovich, Roy Scheider, and Liam Cunningham.

11
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
The film depicts the troubled production behind the 1941 film Citizen Kane.

12
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film's title is a reference to the original
production number of Citizen Kane.

13
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
It premiered on HBO on November 20, 1999.

14
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
The film explores themes of cinema on cinema, yellow press,
movie business, biography, antisemitism.

15
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
The tone is emotional.
